## Workflow for adding a feature

1. **Author** `features/<name>/<name>.lzi` per [Lazuli grammar](https://github.com/lazuli-lang/lazuli/blob/main/docs/grammar.lzi.md).
2. **Surfaces** (if user-facing): `features/<name>/<name>.lzx` (abstract) + `<name>.web.lzx` / `<name>.mobile.lzx` (per audience).
3. **Gate**: `lazuli check . && lazuli doctor .` — MUST be clean before continuing.
4. **Handlers** (if needed): `app/features/<name>/<fn>.go` — `package <name>`; filename matches `@fn.<fn>` reference exactly. Self-register at init via `lazuli.RegisterFn("<feature>.<fn>", <FnName>)` (auto-emitted in scaffolded stubs).
5. **Verify codegen**: `lazuli generate go && go build ./...`.
6. **Re-gate**: `lazuli check . && lazuli doctor .`.

If step 3 or 6 fails: read the diagnostic, fix the `.lzi` (not the workaround). The diagnostic message names the rule code — look it up in your framework docs if unclear.

## Workflow for editing a feature

1. **Inspect first**: `lazuli inspect features/<feature>/<feature>.lzi --format=lazuli --expand=all` to confirm current behavior matches your mental model.
2. **Edit `.lzi`** (never edit `dist/` — it's regen-only).
3. **Re-inspect**: confirm the IR changed the way you expected.
4. **Gate**: `lazuli check . && lazuli doctor .`.
5. **Regen + build**: `lazuli generate go && go build ./...`.

